{{define "_tdd_process"}}TDD PROCESS:
1. Read 09-test-plan.md for the TC-IDs this task must satisfy. For each TC, read the Caller-Path Contract block (entrypoint, lowest mock seam, forbidden mocks, counter-factual).
2. Write failing test first (red) — the test MUST drive the prescribed entrypoint with the prescribed argument shape, must NOT mock above the entrypoint, must NOT touch any seam in the forbidden-mocks list, and must satisfy the counter-factual (would actually fail against an empty/buggy impl, not just pass because the type signature exists).
3. Run the test, confirm it fails for the right reason (the assertion the counter-factual describes — not an import error or fixture bug). Commit the failing test atomically.
4. Implement minimum code to pass (green).
5. Refactor while keeping tests green.
6. Commit when test suite passes.

Tests that mock above the prescribed entrypoint, or use helper-test signatures production never passes, will be rejected at code review.

AGGREGATE-RESULT INVARIANT (when implementing loops or multi-dispatch):
If the implementation processes a collection, the test suite MUST include:
- A test where ALL items fail — verifying the aggregate escalates rather than reporting success with zero results.
- A test where SOME items fail — verifying partial-failure is distinguishable from full-success.
"The loop ran" is not "the loop worked."
{{end}}
